==Battleground==
*1 [[Hannya]] spawns.
*1 [[Cruel Angel Clionel]] spawns as the boss after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Aku Gory]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*3 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 53.33~56.67 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,700f</sup>.
*3 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 66.67~70 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Wicked Cat (Enemy)|Wicked Cat]] spawns after 160 seconds<sup>4,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Aku Gory]] spawns after 253.33 seconds<sup>7,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
One of the most difficult floors in the entirety of Infernal Tower, this stage gets rid of the Gory Darks from the original but adds two Aku Gories, three Aku Doges and Condemned Pengs, and a Wicked Cat. All of these are midrange pushers that force players to lose ground and pave way for the bosses to advance. Any consistent means of fighting or damaging them are obviously helpful, but with Clionel and Hannya's constant attacks from extreme range it becomes quite difficult to keep units alive for long. In order to win, it's important that you kill Hannya as soon as you can, which will often be around the time that Wicked Cat spawns.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] - While there are no Relic threats in this stage, Doron is still useful as a suicide attacker to deliver a burst of damage, mostly concentrated in his level 3 Surge. His extreme health as well as Slow/Weaken Immunity are all points in his favor, and in certain strategies he can be the primary source of offense by sniping the bosses in the backlines or dealing with Condemned Pengs.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] - Bullet Train worked just as well as it did in many Clionel/Hannya stages. Having the Extra Money ability and very high speed at such a low cost, it can be used to deliver a burst of damage to Hannya/Clionel. It can also be used to snipe Doge Darks, although it needs to be at level 47 with a 10% damage combo to do so.
*[[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Cutter Cat]] - Cutter is often the go-to specialist for fighting Hannya. Its low cost, very high speed, full backswing cooldown, Weaken Immunity, 100% survive, 400% Strengthen at 1% health and Massive Damage to Red enemies can dramatically increase its impact by ripping huge chunks of Hannya's health when there are no threats in the way, such as in the beginning. Cutter's 10% damage combo only sweetens the deal further, although its long recharge can be a handful.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]] - With proper timing, Balrog has the opportunity to shred the various threats of this stage. However, if Hannya and Clionel are synchronized, he can get juggled to death without getting anything done. It's not advised to spam him, as he can easily be a drain on your wallet.
*[[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]]: His high speed gets into Clionel's blindspot, Knockback against Angels pushes Clionel away, high HP tanks Hannya's attacks, and immunity to Hannya's Weaken means he does really good DPS to Hannya. Just kill Aku Gory before sending him out.
* [[Knuckles (Uber Rare Cat)|Knuckles]]: Knuckles's high speed lets him cruise into Clionel's blindspot, while his Strong against Red and immunity to Weaken lets him tank Hannya while taking huge chunks of her health. Much like the other Ubers listed, he struggles against the Aku peons, so be sure to remove them before sending Knuckles out.

